script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'spec-fixes-wave2',
  description: 'Fix spec-level audit issues on 36 tasks: tighten verifiers (pin concrete measurements, close coverage), reconcile bleed over-claims to trim-only, and strengthen PHOTO-25 deliverable',
  phases: [{ title: 'Spec fixes' }],
}
const BASE = '/Users/dhiren/Downloads/Deccan/Adobe-Freelance-Leads'
const AUDIT = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-dhiren-Downloads-Deccan/aa9e6dfc-7579-493e-a3a8-45be309ed406/scratchpad/audit_bytask.json'
const IDS = args
const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    task_id: { type: 'string' },
    verifiers_fixed: { type: 'boolean' },
    bleed_fixed: { type: 'boolean' },
    deliverable_strengthened: { type: 'boolean' },
    changes: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    summary: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['task_id', 'changes', 'summary'],
}
const results = await parallel(IDS.map((id) => () => agent(
  `Fix the spec-level audit issues on task ${id}. Edit ONLY ${BASE}/complex_benchmark/adobe_only/specs_v3/${id}.json (valid JSON, preserve every field and everything not explicitly flagged).\n\n` +
  `First read this task's audit entry: open ${AUDIT} (a JSON object keyed by task_id) and read the "${id}" entry — note its verifier_issue, doability_issue, asset_issue, deliverable_issue, and the boolean flags (verifiers_auto_objective, verifiers_human_subjective, verifiers_cover_all).\n` +
  `Also read ${BASE}/input_assets_v3/${id}/asset_plan.json to get concrete pixel dimensions (target_px) and real field values when a verifier needs a number pinned.\n\n` +
  `Apply whichever of these THREE fixes actually apply to ${id}:\n\n` +
  `(A) VERIFIERS — if the audit flags a verifier problem (any of the three verifier flags false, or a verifier_issue): tighten verifiers_auto so EACH one's "how" is a concrete deterministic measurement (pin the exact pixel dimension where a verifier says vague things like "at the retailer's stated tile size" — use the real number from the spec/plan/target_px; give an exact count / hex / string / page-record count). Ensure EVERY deliverable and EVERY emergent_checkpoint has at least one verifier (add one if a gap is named). If any verifiers_auto item actually needs human judgement, move it to verifiers_human; if any verifiers_human item is objectively measurable, move it to verifiers_auto with a concrete "how". Keep all already-good verifiers and their ids unchanged. A human rater must be able to read each verifier + look at the output + grade it.\n\n` +
  `(B) BLEED — scan the spec for any claim of 3mm bleed / "press-ready with bleed" / "trim plus bleed" produced FROM the PDF-derived merge template (in deliverables, trajectory, acceptance_bar, doability_proof). convert_pdf_to_indd sets BleedBox=TrimBox so bleed CANNOT be produced. Rewrite those claims to deliver at TRIM only, and add a short clause noting the connector cannot add bleed to a PDF-derived template (so trim-only is the honest deliverable). Do not remove the merge deliverable itself — only correct the bleed over-claim.\n\n` +
  `(C) DELIVERABLE (only if ${id} is PHOTO-25): the audit flagged its deliverables as weak. Strengthen the weakest deliverable into a real, distinct, hard client output consistent with the brand, adding matching verifier(s). Keep it realistic.\n\n` +
  `If a category does not apply to ${id}, skip it. Report verifiers_fixed / bleed_fixed / deliverable_strengthened booleans, a short changes list, and a one-line summary. Do not touch any other file.`,
  { agentType: 'general-purpose', phase: 'Spec fixes', label: `spec:${id}`, schema: SCHEMA }
)))
const r = results.filter(Boolean)
return {
  tasks: r.length,
  verifiers_fixed: r.filter(x => x.verifiers_fixed).length,
  bleed_fixed: r.filter(x => x.bleed_fixed).length,
  deliverable_strengthened: r.filter(x => x.deliverable_strengthened).map(x => x.task_id),
  per_task: r.map(x => ({ id: x.task_id, summary: x.summary })),
}
